      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "μ4-OH-bridged Tb4 square with a diamagnetic/toroidal ground state (mixed-moment SMT). Room-temperature χMT matches four Tb(III) ions; χMT drops to 4.81 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K. Magnetization rises slowly then steeply near 5 kOe. Micro-SQUID on a single crystal of 1 shows a zero-field plateau below 2 K, narrow hysteresis below 0.5 K, mixed-moment SMT openings of 0.015 Ms at 0.03 K, and QTM at Hc = ±6.4 and 0 kOe. Neighboring Tb magnetic axes are nearly orthogonal (~89.4°). No ac magnetization relaxation.",
        "measurements": [
          {
            "property_type": "magnetic",
            "name": "χMT",
            "value": 47.23,
            "unit": "cm3 K mol−1",
            "conditions": "300 K, 1 kOe, polycrystalline"
          },
          {
            "property_type": "magnetic",
